  "description": "§4.3 (TS14). The route reader's records [x, z, t, t', entry, exit, next-is-0x80-jump] of test 10's route 01 02 03 41 02 0A, and of a route with jumps: a jump to an x-neighbour (6,5)->(7,5) has no exit and blanks (6,5)'s entry in its own record, and (7,5) carries the entry (6,5) had on arrival, -x (TS36, 0x006D666F); a same-cell type change and a jump with dz = -1 give +z; equal magnitudes (-2, -2) zero dx and give -z; (-3, 1) gives -x. The worked example: ConfirmRoute is true when (2,3)'s conn[1] has bit 2, 6, 10 or 14 and (3,3)'s has bit 2 + 4*0; (4,3) is not looked at. A conn bit for another entry fails; the tunnel bit passes; the ferry bit passes with no strike only; a route keeping one type confirms during a strike. The walk-to-bus change at (3,3) (t = 0, t' = 2): during a strike false, otherwise nibble 2 of (3,3)'s switch[0] must be 2. A type change at the first cell needs only the switch nibble, with no strike test. An empty route is false. TS36 in ConfirmRoute: 01 04 03 41 01 02 01 06 03 41 01 02 steps +x into (5,3), jumps to (6,3) and steps +x: (5,3) is skipped (no exit), (6,3) has entry -x (carried) and exit +x, so it needs bit 2 + 4*0 of its conn[1] (with the entry none of the old reading it could pass only on a wormhole bit).",
